<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Attribute Contribution</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h3>Attribute Contribution</h3>
    <p>How much each column actually drove the predictions of <em>this trained model</em>, measured over the test rows. Not a percentage and has no fixed maximum - only meaningful compared to the other columns in this table, higher meaning more influence.</p>
    <p>AGE at 0.42 and REGION at 0.03? This model leans much more heavily on age than region when making a prediction.</p>
    <p>Calculated by averaging <code>PREDICTION_DETAILS</code> (Oracle's per row explanation) across the test set.</p>
</body>
</html>
